Description: An automated surveillance system for infectious disease
    epidemiologists that detects aberrations in laboratory-confirmed
    infections, records epidemiologist's formal assessment with a full
    audit trail, and produces outbreak reports for clinical colleagues
    and infection prevention nurses. Applies evidence-based statistical
    methods such as Improved Farrington (2013)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.5595> and 'EpiEstim' (Cori et al. 2013)
    <doi:10.1093/aje/kwt133>. Ships with a synthetic demo data set
    requiring no external data or infrastructure.
